x}-4x{e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355825 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355825 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "83c85d82-9f4d-5dcd-9620-806a3fb14661" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355955 #edb/ref 1080 "y=3{e}^{-2x}-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355955 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186355955 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "921b7f74-7ba0-5166-ae5f-4fc5433f8be0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356635 #edb/ref 1080 "y={e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356635 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186356635 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1145164-af87-5e30-966d-17507213ec37" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355234 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186355955 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186356635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186356635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357341 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f43be71d-0862-510f-b914-b36421c29d54" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357578 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186357341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357578 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357578 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357578 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny(x)=A{e}^{-2x}+Bx{e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+4\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x,\\,y(0)=-1,\\,{y}^{′}(0)=-2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357578 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "50d3f5fe-3c9a-51a8-8637-85b029f95cf4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186357578 #edb/ref 1074 "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ by substituting the initial conditions.\n\n- Substituting $y(0)=-1$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-1 & =A{e}^{-2(0)}+B(0){e}^{-2(0)}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2(0) \\\\ -1 & =A-2 \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Differentiating $y$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=-2A{e}^{-2x}-2Bx{e}^{-2x}+B{e}^{-2x}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(0)=-2$ into the derivative gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2 & =-2A{e}^{-2(0)}-2B(0){e}^{-2(0)}+B{e}^{-2(0)}+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡2(0) \\\\ -2 & =-2A+B \\\\ -2 & =-2+B \\\\ B & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $A=1$ and $B=0,$ we have the following solution to the initial value problem:\n\n$$\ny={e}^{-2x}-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404440 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186404441 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404440 #edb/ref 1069 "q-8854" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404440 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404440 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+16y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404440 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fe1794bb-4b33-510b-8172-929bfa639d36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404440 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x),$ which is the solution to the homogeneous equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+16y=0.\n$$\n\nWriting down and solving the auxiliary equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}$, and therefore the complementary function ${y}_{c}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{c}(x)=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x).$\n\nThe particular solution of the inhomogeneous equation cannot be of the form $\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x$ because this is already included in the complementary function. Therefore, we assume a particular solution of the form \n\n$$\n{y}_{p}=x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x),\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants that are to be determined. \n\nCalculating the first and second derivatives of ${y}_{p}$ gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}x} & =(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+4x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ \\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}{y}_{p}}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the values of $\\alpha $ and $\\beta ,$ we substitute the derivatives into the differential equation:\n\n$$\n8(-\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x)+16x(-\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x-\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)+16x(\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+\\beta \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\,=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nGrouping the terms on the left-hand side gives\n\n$$\n-8\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+8\\beta \\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\beta =0\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x) \\\\ -8\\alpha =4\\, & (\\text{equating the coefficients of}\\,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x)\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this system gives $\\alpha =-\\frac{1}{2}$, $\\beta =0.$\nTherefore, the particular solution ${y}_{p}(x)$ is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(x)=-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$\n\nThe general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nand therefore, the general solution in our case is\n\n$$\ny={y}_{c}+{y}_{p}=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186404446 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186404443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404441 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9dec29b5-6835-594f-89d3-a76d54e5866b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404442 #edb/ref 1080 "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404442 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404442 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5e77e8eb-4f76-565b-b3a2-5c91767ba39f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404443 #edb/ref 1080 "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x-\\frac{1}{2}x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404443 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404443 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "de87823a-03c0-572e-9778-3d0e131e7ba6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404444 #edb/ref 1080 "y=P\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+Q\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404444 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186404444 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "edee0d23-5e90-53e9-9a9b-3e624f83441e" #edb/ref 175921